%27ing_Period/Ch%27%C3%AAn_Chuan\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Ch&#39;\u00ean Chuan\">Ch'\u00ean Chuan</a></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward-arrow\">\u2192</div></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-notes header&#95;notes searchaux wst-unknown-notes\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14791120\">.mw-parser-output .plainSister{display:block;font-size:93%;line-height:normal;list-style-type:none;list-style-image:none;list-style-position:outside;border:1px solid var(--border-color-interactive--hover,#AAA);float:right;clear:right;margin:0.5ex 0 0.5ex 0.5ex;padding:0;background:var(--background-color-base,#FFFFFF);color:var(--color-base,#202122)}.mw-parser-output .sisicon,.mw-parser-output .dabicon{padding-right:1ex}</style><ul class=\"plainSister\"><li class=\"sisitem\"><span class=\"sisicon\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\"><img alt=\"Sister Projects\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/20px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/40px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\">sister projects</a>: <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q107367036\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q107367036\">Wikidata item</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"ws-noexport\" id=\"ws-data\" style=\"speak:none\"><span id=\"ws-article-id\">3633518</span><span id=\"ws-title\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period\">Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period</a>, Volume 1 \u2014 Ch&#39;\u00ean Ch&#39;i-y\u00fcan</span><span id=\"ws-editor\">Arthur W. Hummel</span><span id=\"ws-author\">Earl Swisher</span></div></div>\n<p><span style=\"display:none\" id=\"dynamic&#95;layout&#95;overrider\">Layout 2</span>\n</p>\n<div class=\"prp-pages-output\" lang=\"en\">\n<p><span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"85\" data-page-number=\"85\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 1.pdf/97\" data-page-index=\"97\" data-page-quality=\"4\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;1.pdf/97\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;97\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span><b>CH'\u00caN</b> Ch'i-y\u00fcan \u9673\u555f\u6e90 (<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14767791\">.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip{cursor:help;border-bottom:thin dotted cornflowerblue}.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip-nodash{border-bottom:none}</style><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u9577\u767c,&#32;<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Literary name (Hao, \u865f)\">H.</span>&#160;\u898b\u6843\u5c45\u58eb), d. 1689, scholar, was a native of Wu-chiang, Kiangsu, and a close friend of Chu Ho-ling \u6731\u9db4\u9f61 (<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u9577\u5b7a,&#32;<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Literary name (Hao, \u865f)\">H.</span>&#160;\u611a\u83f4,&#32;1606\u20131683) of the same locality. A licentiate, he collaborated with the latter in the compilation of a comprehensive study of the <i><a href=\"/wiki/Classic_of_Poetry\" class=\"mw-disambig\" title=\"Classic of Poetry\">Odes</a></i>, entitled \u6bdb\u8a69\u901a\u7fa9 <i>Mao-shih t'ung-i</i>, in 12 <i>ch\u00fcan</i>, which is regarded as inferior to his own critical study of the <i>Odes</i> based on the exposition of pre-T'ang scholars. This latter \u6bdb\u8a69\u7a3d\u53e4\u7de8 <i>Mao-shih chi-ku pien</i>, 30 <i>ch\u00fcan</i>, was completed in 1687 after 14 years of labor and was first published in 1813 with a preface by <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Juan_Y%C3%BCan\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Juan Y\u00fcan\">Juan Y\u00fcan</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>]. It was copied into the <i>Imperial Library</i> (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Chi_Y%C3%BCn\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Chi Y\u00fcn\">Chi Y\u00fcn</a></span>) and is included in the <i>Huang-Ch'ing ching-chieh</i> (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Juan_Y%C3%BCan\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Juan Y\u00fcan\">Juan Y\u00fcan</a></span>). In it Ch'\u00ean Ch'i-y\u00fcan analyzes and corrects the works on the <i>Odes</i> by <a href=\"/wiki/Author:Zhu_Xi\" title=\"Author:Zhu Xi\">Chu Hsi</a> (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Hu_Wei\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Hu Wei\">Hu Wei</a></span>), Ou-yang Hsiu (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Shao_Chin-han\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Shao Chin-han\">Shao Chin-han</a></span>), L\u00fc Tsu-ch'ien \u5442\u7956\u8b19 (1137-1181), and Yen Ts'an \u56b4\u7cb2 (13th century), and attacks those of Liu Chin \u5289\u747e (Y\u00fcan dynasty), and Fu Kuang \u8f14\u5ee3 (Sung dynasty). It is one of the best examples of the beginnings of scientific study of the classics in the early Ch'ing period. A Buddhist believer, he has been charged with religious leanings in some of his interpretations and even with having been influenced indirectly by the Jesuits.\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431518\">.mw-parser-output .wst-rule{background-color:currentcolor;color:inherit;width:auto;margin:2px auto 2px auto;height:1px;overflow:hidden}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-left{margin-left:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-right{margin-right:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.__uirule{background-color:#a2a9b1;color:inherit;border:0;margin-top:0.2em;margin-bottom:0.2em}</style><hr class=\"wst-rule wst-rule-left\" style=\"color:inherit;width:40%;\" />\n<p>[1/486/16a; 2/68/6b; 3;413/24a; 7/32/15a; 16/12/4a; 17/3/46a; 23/3/25a; \u5c0f\u8146\u7d00\u50b3 <i>Hsiao-t'ien chi-chuan</i> 53/19b; <i>Ss\u016d-k'u</i> (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Chi_Y%C3%BCn\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Chi Y\u00fcn\">Chi Y\u00fcn</a></span>), 16/6a; Legge, <i>Chinese Classics</i>, IV, I, p. 177, but mistaken in date of publication; year of death in one of the prefaces to <i>Mao-shih chi-ku pien</i>]\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431519\">.mw-parser-output .wst-right{text-align:right}</style><div class=\"wst-right\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\">\n<p><span class=\"smallcaps\" style=\"font-variant:small-caps;\">Earl Swisher</span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p><br />\n&#32;\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>"},"links":[{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Classic of Poetry"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Ch'\u00ean Ch'i-y\u00fc"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Ch'\u00ean Chuan"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Chi Y\u00fcn"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Hu Wei"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Juan Y\u00fcan"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Shao Chin-han"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Arthur W. Hummel"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Earl Swisher"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Zhu Xi"}],"sections":[],"wikitext":{"*":"{{Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period\n | volume   = 1\n | onlysection = ch'en ch'i-yuan\n | previous = Ch'\u00ean Ch'i-y\u00fc\n | next     = Ch'\u00ean Chuan\n | from     = 97\n | to       = 97\n | notes    = \n | section_author = Earl Swisher\n}}{{DEFAULTSORT:Ch'\u00ean Ch'i-y\u00fcan}}"}}}